  "body": "## What changed\n\nPR #1689 moved the orthographic near plane far behind the eye. The ortho eye sits only `ORTHO_EYE_DIST` (100 mm) in front of the target, and the near plane is `(dist * 20).max(1000) - 100` mm behind the eye. But `Camera::ray_through` still started the ortho ray on the eye plane. Thus a face nearer the viewer than the eye plane was drawn, but a click passed it.\n\nExample (the new test): a top view in ortho, and a 300 mm column on Z 0. The view draws the top face at Z 300. Before this change, the click ray started at Z 100, inside the column, and `pick::first_hit_f` found the bottom face at Z 0.\n\n- `crates/ui/src/viewport.rs`:\n  - New helper `Camera::ortho_behind_eye()`: the near-plane offset behind the eye plane, in mm.\n  - `Camera::mvp` uses it for the ortho `near` (the same value as before).\n  - `Camera::ray_through` (ortho branch) moves the origin back by that offset along the view direction. The direction and the line of the ray do not change. The doc comment says so.\n- `crates/ui/src/ortho_pick_tests.rs`: two new tests (registered in `lib.rs`).\n\nWhy the other ray users are safe (they use the same line, not the old origin point):\n- `interact::pick_model` and `feature_click::query_at`: nearest hit along the ray. In ortho the pick radius is one fixed value (`radius_per_depth` is 0), so a farther origin does not change it.\n- `move_drag::axis_t`, `turn_drag::plane_angle`: an axis or a plane intersection of the line.\n- `box_pick`: the ortho occlusion test uses the view direction.\n- The ortho tests in `law_tests.rs` (cursor closure, mode switch, ortho dolly) project points of the ray. In ortho the screen position does not depend on depth.\n\n## Tests\n\nPinned by (`camcraft-ui` lib, `ortho_pick_tests`):\n- `an_ortho_pick_hits_the_top_face_that_stands_above_the_eye_plane`: the click finds `Column` at Z 300.\n- `the_ortho_ray_starts_on_the_near_plane_and_keeps_its_line`: for three cursor points the origin is `ortho_behind_eye` behind the eye plane and the rays are parallel; a point on that plane maps to clip depth 0 through `mvp`, so the matrix and the ray agree.\n\nWith the old origin (`back = 0`), both tests fail: `the nearest face is the top at Z 300, not [.., 0.0]` and `origin [.., 100.0]`.\n\nQuick gate (`cargo xtask gate quick --base upstream/main`, Linux, 12 cores, another build running on the box):\n- `ui build (--no-run)`: ok.\n- `ui suites: lib`: 1204 passed, 0 failed (both new tests included).\n- `ui suites: catalog_render`, `ui suites: gpu_render`: ok.\n\n`cargo clippy -p camcraft-ui --all-targets -- -D warnings`: clean.\n\n## Not exercised\n\n- No click in the running app. The tests use the same two calls as `interact::pick_model` (`Camera::ray_through`, then `pick::first_hit_f`).\n- Perspective picking does not change.\n\n## Notes\n\n- `viewport.rs` is already longer than 400 lines. The change adds 9 lines net (+16, -7), of which 7 are the helper and its doc. The tests are in a new file.\n- Branch base: `upstream/main`. No context scout ran; this session did its own searches.\n\nChangelog: Orthographic view: a click picks a face that is nearer the viewer than the camera eye plane (for example the top of a tall part), not the face behind it.\nEffort: low\n\nFixes #2375\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
